1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:01,264
For 20 minutes,

2
00:00:01,264 --> 00:00:02,727
a burning ship drifted through

3
00:00:02,727 --> 00:00:05,026
Halifax harbour, and thousands stopped

4
00:00:05,026 --> 00:00:06,778
at their windows to watch.

5
00:00:07,413 --> 00:00:08,772
The French ship Mont-Blanc was

6
00:00:08,772 --> 00:00:10,014
full of TNT,

7
00:00:10,014 --> 00:00:11,813
picric acid and benzol,

8
00:00:11,973 --> 00:00:13,102
and had just collided with

9
00:00:13,102 --> 00:00:13,864
the Imo.

10
00:00:14,453 --> 00:00:16,171
Dispatcher Vince Coleman stayed at

11
00:00:16,171 --> 00:00:18,283
his telegraph to stop the trains.

12
00:00:18,486 --> 00:00:20,036
He died at his post.

13
00:00:21,683 --> 00:00:24,445
At 9:04, Mont-Blanc exploded:

14
00:00:24,516 --> 00:00:26,246
the largest man-made blast the

15
00:00:26,246 --> 00:00:27,917
world had ever seen.

16
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:30,980
Nearly everything within 800 metres

17
00:00:30,980 --> 00:00:31,896
was flattened.

18
00:00:31,932 --> 00:00:34,831
At least 1,782 people died.

19
00:00:36,227 --> 00:00:38,386
Every year since 1971,

20
00:00:38,386 --> 00:00:39,919
Nova Scotia has sent Boston

21
00:00:39,919 --> 00:00:40,963
a Christmas tree.

22
00:00:41,068 --> 00:00:42,646
It still says thank you.
